  "query_preview": "..\nKEY MESSAGE 1...Dry and tranquil weather will continue through this \nweekend.\n\nHigh pressure will continue to dominate the weather across our \nregion through the weekend. A moisture-starved cold front will \ncontinue to move south and away from the area this evening. Behind \nthe front, an incoming cooler air mass will bring some increase in \nlake-induced instability, with low level north to northeast flow \nproducing a brief period of lake effect and upslope clouds tonight. \nThese clouds will already have scattered out before daybreak Friday.\n\nHigh pressure at the surface and aloft will continue to build to\nthe east and settle over the Northeast Friday and this weekend.\nDry weather and clear to partly cloudy sky are expected as \nstabilizing subsidence accompanies the ridge. Daily highs should\nmoderate from mainly the 50s to 60F Friday to the mid 50s to upper\n60s on Sunday as a more southerly flow develops on the western \nside of the ridge.\n\nThe environment should remain favorable for localized and shallow \nfog in the Black River Valley, Western Southern Tier river valleys, \nand the lake valleys of the Finger Lakes Region between about \nmidnight and 9 AM EDT Saturday through Sunday.",
